# Where the API lives.
#
# Leave this EMPTY. The client then calls same-origin "/api", which is correct
# everywhere it runs:
#
#   development  Vite proxies /api to VITE_API_TARGET below.
#   production   Vercel rewrites /api to the Tailscale Funnel in front of the
#                machine that holds the database (see frontend/vercel.json).
#   direct       The API process also serves the built app, so opening the
#                tunnel address itself works without any of the above.
#
# One build works in all three, and the browser only ever talks to one origin,
# so there is no CORS preflight on every request.
#
# Set it to an absolute URL only if the app is ever hosted somewhere the API is
# not reachable from. Vite bakes VITE_* values in at BUILD time, so changing it
# needs a rebuild rather than a restart -- which is exactly why the API address
# lives in a Vercel rewrite instead of in here.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Dev-only: where the Vite proxy forwards /api during `npm run dev`.
VITE_API_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000
